EXPERIMENT 52 – SYSTEM TESTING OF END-TO-END CHECKOUT FLOW USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to execute system testing of an end-to-end checkout flow.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Login with a valid user on the demo shopping website.
3. Add the Backpack to the cart and verify that the cart badge shows 1.
4. Open the cart and click Checkout.
5. Enter first name, last name and postal code, then click Continue.
6. Click Finish and verify the order confirmation message.
7. Display the system test result.
CODE
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise52 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();
            driver.get("https://www.saucedemo.com");

            driver.findElement(By.id("user-name"))
                .sendKeys("standard_user");

            driver.findElement(By.id("password"))
                .sendKeys("secret_sauce");

            driver.findElement(By.id("login-button")).click();

            driver.findElement(
                By.id("add-to-cart-sauce-labs-backpack")).click();

            String badge = driver.findElement(
                By.className("shopping_cart_badge")).getText();

            System.out.println("Cart badge count : " + badge);

            driver.findElement(
                By.className("shopping_cart_link")).click();

            driver.findElement(By.id("checkout")).click();

            driver.findElement(By.id("first-name")).sendKeys("Test");
            driver.findElement(By.id("last-name")).sendKeys("User");
            driver.findElement(By.id("postal-code")).sendKeys("600001");

            driver.findElement(By.id("continue")).click();
            driver.findElement(By.id("finish")).click();

            String status = driver.findElement(
                By.className("complete-header")).getText();

            System.out.println("Order status     : " + status);

            System.out.println("System test      : "
                + (badge.equals("1") &&
                status.equals("Thank you for your order!")
                ? "PASS" : "FAIL"));

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- URL: https://www.saucedemo.com
- Username: standard_user
- Password: secret_sauce
- Product: Sauce Labs Backpack
- First name: Test
- Last name: User
- Postal code: 600001
OUTPUT
Cart badge count : 1
Order status     : Thank you for your order!
System test      : PASS


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to execute system testing of an end-to-end checkout flow was executed successfully, and the output was verified.
